                <pb facs="0841" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/15432.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-16T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 16, 1915—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>819. Your 672, July 13, 5 p.m. The attitude assumed by General Gonzalez since his
                    occupation of Mexico City has made a favorable impression upon this Government
                    and it is hoped nothing will arise to deter him from his good purposes.</p>
                <p>You may inform General Gonzalez that this message is being copied to Silliman for
                    information General Carranza.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
